From b13e950d9445ffdcb05333c056b4a36825f40fc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kkutysllb <46704313+kkutysllb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 23:54:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui-chat,ui-conversation): revive sent-message edit as
 composer draft refill

A transcript edit entry on user bubbles disappeared with the retired
attachment-plugin host patch chain; upstream never shipped message
editing (#3452 was added and reverted the same day). Restore the common
gesture as an engine-side, UI-only feature: an edit action on durable
user bubbles replaces the composer draft with that message's text (the
user revises and resends a new turn), leaving session storage and the
agent loop untouched.

- ui-conversation: scope-addressed ctx.conversation.fillDraft(text)
  resolves the caller session's input shell and rewrites the whole draft
  (SessionInput.setDraft, which lands the caret at the end).
- ui-chat: ChatViewInjected/ChatNodeOwnerProps gain editUserMessage,
  wired in apply() over the session binding ctx; MessageIconActions
  gains an optional onEdit control (pencil, copy position); the user/
  steering message view passes the bubble text through.
- i18n zh/en, plus one component spec per package.

Client specs: ui-chat 51/51 + ui-conversation fill-draft; oxlint clean.
Wiring-level typecheck rides the release build (workspace libs are
stale without it).
